    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Early settlers left petroglyphs and artifacts in the valley’s caves, making Beulah one of the first settlements in the Wet Mountains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.uncovercolorado.com/towns/beulah-valley/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Archaeologists have uncovered evidence that Confederate Army troops once used a headquarters in Beulah during the Civil War.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.uncovercolorado.com/towns/beulah-valley/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Between Beulah and San Isabel stands Bishop Castle, a one‑man construction by Jim Bishop that still towers over the valley.",
